## How a theme colour choice works

1. The person picks a colour with **Theme colour**, or selects a Civica theme in the native theme selector.
2. **Theme colour** shows the colour of the current theme.
3. Changing it selects the matching generated theme, such as `Civica Teal`.
4. A short status message reports the selection, for example “Teal theme colour selected.” Home Assistant applies and saves the theme. The message does not confirm that the save finished.

The real control has no Save button. The preview above adds a “Preview saving” button so it can show feedback locally.

Keep focus on the control. Do not move to another page, reload or ask for confirmation. Do not change another user’s settings. Do not use Home Assistant’s default-theme action for a personal preference.

## Keep the native controls

The native theme selector and the Light, Dark or Auto setting stay available. If the person uses the native selector, the Civica controls must show the same theme.

Choosing a theme colour clears any custom primary or accent colour, so an old override cannot hide the new colour. Say so in the help text or in [Change theme colours](../get-started/colour-settings.html).

## When it cannot apply

- **A Civica theme is missing, themes are loading, or Home Assistant is in safe or recovery mode:** keep the current theme and show the message given in [Errors and recovery](recovery.html). That page owns the wording.
- **The profile page changes:** fail safely and offer the standalone settings card. Never hide the native settings because the controls did not find their place. [Change theme colours](../get-started/colour-settings.html) shows the card.

## Keep the scope narrow

The preview on this site changes only itself. The Home Assistant module changes only the signed-in person’s chosen theme through the native flow. Neither changes the colour of a light or any other device.

## Test the preference

Check the controls by keyboard and with a screen reader, at 320 CSS pixels and larger text. Check that the status message is announced once. Switch themes with the native selector and confirm the Civica controls follow. Repeat with a missing theme and in safe mode.
